    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_10",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Victor Heerman (August 27, 1893 – November 3, 1977) was an English-American screenwriter, film director, and film producer. After writing and directing short comedies for Mack Sennett, Heerman teamed with his wife Sarah Y. Mason to win the Academy Award for best screenplay adaptation of Louisa May Alcott's novel \"Little Women\" in 1933. He directed the Marx Brothers' second film, \"Animal Crackers\", in 1930.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.9999999956692394,
      "temperature": 0.9999999956692394,
      "expanded": false,
